# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vkey
# `.vkey` alone is an exact match. The trailing * covers per-scenario key files
# (.vkey.budget-test) and backups, which are the same secret in another name.
.vkey*
vkey.json
vkey*.json
*.key
*.pem
*credentials*
*secret*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Captured traffic — never commit
#
# Captures contain the full text of prompts, file contents, and command output
# returned to the model in tool_result blocks. Treat the capture store as
# confidential data, not as source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
capture/
capture_archive/
export/
_kwargs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reference documentation — kept locally, not committed
#
# The PoC overview deck is guidance to follow while building, not source. It is
# distributed by hand rather than versioned here.
#
# NOTE: this file was already tracked, so ignoring it is not enough on its own —
# it was untracked with `git rm --cached` in the same commit that added this rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Emumba_PoC_Enterprise_Control_Plane.html
#
# The status deck (docs/Emumba_PoC_Status_Report.html) and the condensed flows
# deck (docs/Emumba_PoC_Flows_What_How.html) ARE tracked. They are generated
# from docs/PROJECT-STATUS.md and docs/skills-flow.md, which stay the source of
# truth — regenerate and commit the decks whenever the Markdown changes, or the
# copies drift.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local / OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
*.log
